  "text": "\nSummary of the migration:\n\n## Analysis\n\n| File | Usage | Eligible? |\n|------|-------|-----------|\n| **CreateNewButton.tsx** | `locationService.push` after creating a folder | Yes – React component |\n| **FolderActionsButton.tsx** | `locationService.push` after deleting a folder | Yes – React component |\n| **browseDashboardsAPI.ts** | `locationService.push` in `importDashboard` mutation's `queryFulfilled` | No – RTK Query API slice, not a React component; hooks cannot be used here |\n\n## Changes made\n\n### 1. Feature flag\n\nAdded `browseDashboardsUseNavigate` in `pkg/services/featuremgmt/registry.go`:\n\n```go\n{\n    Name:         \"browseDashboardsUseNavigate\",\n    Description:  \"Use React Router's useNavigate hook instead of locationService in browse dashboards pages\",\n    Stage:        FeatureStageExperimental,\n    FrontendOnly: true,\n    Owner:        grafanaDashboardsSquad,\n    Expression:   \"false\",\n},\n```\n\n### 2. CreateNewButton.tsx\n\n- Imported `useNavigate` from `react-router-dom-v5-compat`\n- Called `useNavigate()` at the top of the component\n- Wrapped navigation after folder creation with the feature flag:\n\n```typescript\nif (config.featureToggles.browseDashboardsUseNavigate) {\n  navigate(url);\n} else {\n  locationService.push(url);\n}\n```\n\n### 3. FolderActionsButton.tsx\n\n- Imported `useNavigate` and `config`\n- Called `useNavigate()` at the top of the component\n- Wrapped navigation after folder deletion with the same feature-flag pattern\n\n### 4. browseDashboardsAPI.ts\n\nLeft as-is. It runs inside RTK Query middleware, outside React, so `useNavigate` cannot be used. Navigation after import continues to use `locationService.push`.\n\n## Next step\n\nRun feature toggle generation so the new flag is included in the generated types:\n\n```bash\nmake gen-feature-toggles\n```\n\nThis updates `packages/grafana-data/src/types/featureToggles.gen.ts`, `toggles_gen.json`, and related files. The frontend build completed successfully with the current changes.",
