  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "The implementation is complete and lint-free. Here's a summary of what was added:\n\n### Category Assignment (`assignCategory`)\nBookmarks are automatically categorized by their URL patterns:\n- **Operations** (warning-colored cards, bell icon) -- alerting, connections, monitoring, infrastructure, incidents, correlations\n- **Admin** (secondary-colored cards, cog icon) -- admin, org, profile, plugins, users, teams, service accounts, API keys\n- **Content** (primary-colored cards, apps icon) -- everything else (dashboards, explore, playlists, etc.)\n\n### Filtering UI\n- **`FilterInput`** at the top for free-text search across bookmark name and description\n- **`RadioButtonGroup`** with All / Operations / Admin / Content toggles to filter by category\n\n### Grouped Display\n- Bookmarks are grouped into sections with a header showing the category icon, label, and count\n- Each section renders its cards in the existing responsive grid layout\n- Empty groups are automatically hidden\n- When no bookmarks match the current filter, a \"not found\" empty state is shown\n- The original \"no bookmarks yet\" empty state is preserved for when there are zero pinned items\n\nAll components used (`FilterInput`, `RadioButtonGroup`, `Stack`, `Icon`, `EmptyState`) are standard `@grafana/ui` components, and the patterns follow existing Grafana list pages like `UserListAdminPage`.",
