  "text": "Here are the three diagrams.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Relationship Between `locationService` and React Router\n\nThis shows the ownership and data-flow relationship between the singleton `locationService`, the `history` library, and the React Router component tree.\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TB\n    subgraph \"Singleton (module-level)\"\n        LS[\"locationService<br/><i>HistoryWrapper</i>\"]\n        H[\"history<br/><i>H.createBrowserHistory()</i>\"]\n        BS[\"BehaviorSubject&lt;Location&gt;<br/><i>locationObservable</i>\"]\n    end\n\n    LS -->|\"owns\"| H\n    LS -->|\"owns\"| BS\n    H -->|\"history.listen()\"| BS\n\n    subgraph \"React Component Tree\"\n        RW[\"RouterWrapper<br/><i>RoutesWrapper.tsx</i>\"]\n        R5[\"&lt;Router&gt;<br/><i>react-router-dom v5</i>\"]\n        LSP[\"&lt;LocationServiceProvider&gt;<br/><i>React Context</i>\"]\n        CR[\"&lt;CompatRouter&gt;<br/><i>react-router-dom-v5-compat</i>\"]\n        ROUTES[\"&lt;Routes&gt; + &lt;Route&gt;<br/><i>v6 API via compat</i>\"]\n        GRW[\"GrafanaRouteWrapper<br/><i>auth, RBAC checks</i>\"]\n        GR[\"GrafanaRoute<br/><i>error boundary, pageview</i>\"]\n        FC[\"Feature Component<br/><i>lazy-loaded</i>\"]\n    end\n\n    LS -->|\"getHistory()\"| R5\n    LS -->|\"provided via context\"| LSP\n\n    RW --> R5\n    R5 --> LSP\n    LSP --> CR\n    CR --> ROUTES\n    ROUTES --> GRW\n    GRW --> GR\n    GR --> FC\n\n    subgraph \"Imperative Callers (legacy v5 pattern)\"\n        IC1[\"locationService.push()\"]\n        IC2[\"locationService.partial()\"]\n        IC3[\"locationService.replace()\"]\n        IC4[\"interceptLinkClicks()\"]\n    end\n\n    IC1 -->|\"history.push()\"| H\n    IC2 -->|\"history.push/replace()\"| H\n    IC3 -->|\"history.replace()\"| H\n    IC4 -->|\"locationService.push()\"| LS\n\n    subgraph \"Declarative Callers (v6 pattern)\"\n        DC1[\"useNavigate()\"]\n        DC2[\"useLocation()\"]\n        DC3[\"useParams()\"]\n        DC4[\"&lt;Navigate /&gt;\"]\n    end\n\n    CR -->|\"provides v6 context\"| DC1\n    CR -->|\"provides v6 context\"| DC2\n    CR -->|\"provides v6 context\"| DC3\n    CR -->|\"provides v6 context\"| DC4\n\n    H -->|\"URL changes propagate<br/>back through Router\"| R5\n\n    style LS fill:#f9f,stroke:#333,stroke-width:2px\n    style H fill:#ff9,stroke:#333,stroke-width:2px\n    style CR fill:#9ff,stroke:#333,stroke-width:2px\n```\n\nThe key insight: **both** the legacy `locationService` path and the new `useNavigate` path ultimately funnel through the same `history` object. `locationService` calls `history.push/replace` directly; `useNavigate` (via `CompatRouter`) writes to the same history. The v5 `<Router>` listens to that history and triggers re-renders either way.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Navigation Flow: User Action to URL Change\n\nThis traces the two parallel navigation paths — legacy imperative and modern declarative — from a user action all the way to a URL change and component re-render.\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant User\n    participant DOM as DOM / <a> tag\n    participant ILC as interceptLinkClicks\n    participant LS as locationService\n    participant Hist as history (H.History)\n    participant Browser as Browser URL Bar\n    participant Router as <Router> (v5)\n    participant Compat as <CompatRouter>\n    participant Routes as <Routes>/<Route> (v6)\n    participant GRW as GrafanaRouteWrapper\n    participant Page as Feature Page\n\n    Note over User,Page: PATH A — Legacy (locationService)\n\n    User->>DOM: clicks <a href=\"/dashboards\">\n    DOM->>ILC: MouseEvent (document listener)\n    ILC->>ILC: preventDefault()\n    ILC->>LS: locationService.push(\"/dashboards\")\n    LS->>Hist: history.push(\"/dashboards\")\n    Hist->>Browser: pushState → URL updates\n    Hist->>Router: history listener fires\n    Router->>Compat: re-render children\n    Compat->>Routes: match route\n    Routes->>GRW: render matched <Route>\n    GRW->>GRW: auth + RBAC check\n    GRW->>Page: render component\n\n    Note over User,Page: PATH A variant — Button onClick\n\n    User->>LS: onClick → locationService.push(\"/admin\")\n    LS->>Hist: history.push(\"/admin\")\n    Hist->>Browser: pushState → URL updates\n    Hist->>Router: history listener fires\n    Router->>Page: re-render chain\n\n    Note over User,Page: PATH B — Modern (useNavigate)\n\n    User->>Page: clicks button\n    Page->>Compat: navigate(\"/explore\") via useNavigate()\n    Compat->>Hist: history.push(\"/explore\")\n    Hist->>Browser: pushState → URL updates\n    Hist->>Router: history listener fires\n    Router->>Page: re-render chain\n```\n\nBoth paths converge at the same `history` object. The `CompatRouter` layer ensures that `useNavigate()` writes to the same v5 `history` instance that powers `<Router>`.\n\n---\n\n### 3. The v5-to-v6 Compatibility Layer\n\nThis shows how the `react-router-dom-v5-compat` package bridges the two worlds.\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TB\n    subgraph \"React Router v5 (installed)\"\n        V5R[\"&lt;Router&gt;<br/><i>react-router-dom@5.3.4</i>\"]\n        V5Hist[\"history@4.x<br/><i>H.createBrowserHistory()</i>\"]\n        V5Ctx[\"v5 Router Context<br/><i>match, location, history</i>\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Compatibility Bridge\"\n        COMPAT[\"&lt;CompatRouter&gt;<br/><i>react-router-dom-v5-compat@6.26</i>\"]\n        SYNC[\"Reads v5 context<br/>Writes v6 context\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"v6 APIs (available via compat)\"\n        V6ROUTES[\"&lt;Routes&gt; / &lt;Route&gt;<br/><i>element prop, nested routes</i>\"]\n        V6NAV[\"useNavigate()\"]\n        V6LOC[\"useLocation()\"]\n        V6PAR[\"useParams()\"]\n        V6NAVIGATE[\"&lt;Navigate /&gt;\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"locationService (legacy bridge)\"\n        LS_PUSH[\"locationService.push()\"]\n        LS_PARTIAL[\"locationService.partial()\"]\n        LS_REPLACE[\"locationService.replace()\"]\n    end\n\n    V5Hist -->|\"passed as prop\"| V5R\n    V5R -->|\"provides\"| V5Ctx\n    V5Ctx -->|\"consumed by\"| COMPAT\n    COMPAT -->|\"syncs into\"| SYNC\n    SYNC -->|\"provides v6 context to\"| V6ROUTES\n    SYNC -->|\"provides v6 context to\"| V6NAV\n    SYNC -->|\"provides v6 context to\"| V6LOC\n    SYNC -->|\"provides v6 context to\"| V6PAR\n    SYNC -->|\"provides v6 context to\"| V6NAVIGATE\n\n    LS_PUSH -->|\"writes to\"| V5Hist\n    LS_PARTIAL -->|\"writes to\"| V5Hist\n    LS_REPLACE -->|\"writes to\"| V5Hist\n\n    V6NAV -->|\"writes to<br/>same history\"| V5Hist\n\n    subgraph \"Migration Per Feature\"\n        direction LR\n        FF[\"Feature Flag<br/><i>config.featureToggles.XUseNavigate</i>\"]\n        OLD[\"locationService.push()\"]\n        NEW[\"navigate() via useNavigate()\"]\n        FF -->|\"false\"| OLD\n        FF -->|\"true\"| NEW\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Plugin Compatibility\"\n        P5[\"Plugin uses<br/>react-router-dom (v5)\"]\n        P6[\"Plugin uses<br/>react-router-dom-v5-compat (v6)\"]\n    end\n\n    V5Ctx -->|\"still works\"| P5\n    SYNC -->|\"also works\"| P6\n\n    style COMPAT fill:#9ff,stroke:#333,stroke-width:2px\n    style SYNC fill:#9ff,stroke:#333,stroke-width:1px\n    style FF fill:#ffa,stroke:#333,stroke-width:2px\n```\n\n#### How the compat layer works in practice\n\n1. **`<Router history={locationService.getHistory()}>`** — the v5 `Router` owns the `history` object and provides the v5 router context (match, location, history props).\n\n2. **`<CompatRouter>`** — sits inside the v5 `Router`, reads the v5 context, and re-provides it as a v6-shaped context. This is what makes `useNavigate()`, `useLocation()`, `useParams()`, and `<Routes>`/`<Route element={}>` work inside a v5 app.\n\n3. **Both old and new write to the same history** — `locationService.push()` calls `history.push()` directly. `useNavigate()` (via compat) also calls the same `history.push()`. The v5 `<Router>` listens to that history and triggers re-renders regardless of which caller initiated the change.\n\n4. **Feature flags control the cutover** — each feature area has a toggle like `playlistUseNavigate`. When `true`, the component uses `useNavigate()`; when `false`, it falls back to `locationService.push()`. Once validated, the flag and old code path are removed.\n\n5. **Plugins are insulated** — the `sharedDependencies` loader exposes both `react-router-dom` (v5) and `react-router-dom-v5-compat` to plugins, so plugins can migrate independently.\n\nThe end state, once every feature and shared utility is migrated, is to remove `locationService` entirely, drop the v5 `react-router-dom` dependency, replace `<Router>` + `<CompatRouter>` with a native v6 `<BrowserRouter>`, and run on `react-router-dom@6` directly.",
