{
  "conversation_id": "f203e7e6-ec30-434e-90eb-11ba049cbdb8",
  "generation_id": "053bfee8-d3dc-4cae-8c8a-b5a244b95d83",
  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "Here's a comprehensive overview.\n\n---\n\n## Grafana Codebase Overview\n\nGrafana is a large **monorepo** with a Go backend and a React/TypeScript frontend, managed with Yarn workspaces and Nx.\n\n### Top-Level Structure\n\n| Directory | Purpose |\n|-----------|---------|\n| `public/app/` | Frontend React/TypeScript application |\n| `pkg/` | Backend Go packages and shared libraries |\n| `apps/` | Backend microservices (alerting, dashboards, IAM, etc.) |\n| `packages/` | Shared npm packages (`@grafana/ui`, `@grafana/data`, `@grafana/runtime`, etc.) |\n| `conf/` | Configuration files and templates |\n| `e2e-playwright/` | Playwright end-to-end tests |\n| `devenv/` | Development environment setup |\n| `scripts/` | Build and development scripts |\n| `kinds/` / `kindsv2/` | Kubernetes resource definitions |\n\n### Frontend (`public/app/`)\n\n- **`routes/`** -- Route definitions and router setup\n- **`features/`** -- Feature modules (dashboards, panels, alerting, playlists, etc.)\n- **`core/`** -- Core infrastructure (navigation, state, services)\n- **`plugins/`** -- Built-in datasource and panel plugins\n- **`api/`** -- API client code\n- **`store/`** -- Redux store configuration\n\n### Backend (`pkg/`)\n\n- **`api/`** -- HTTP API handlers\n- **`apiserver/`** -- Kubernetes-style API server\n- **`services/`** -- Business logic services (users, dashboards, alerting, etc.)\n- **`plugins/`** -- Plugin system backend\n- **`middleware/`** -- HTTP middleware (auth, logging, etc.)\n- **`tsdb/`** -- Time-series database abstractions\n\n---\n\n## React Router Architecture\n\n### The Big Picture\n\nGrafana uses **React Router v5** with a **v6 compatibility layer** (`react-router-dom-v5-compat`). This enables incremental migration from the legacy `locationService` singleton to React Router's `useNavigate` hook. The migration is roughly 40% complete.\n\nThe component tree looks like this:\n\n```\nAppWrapper (public/app/AppWrapper.tsx)\n  └── RouterWrapper (public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx)\n        ├── Router (v5, history from locationService)\n        ├── LocationServiceProvider\n        ├── CompatRouter (v5→v6 bridge)\n        └── Routes (v6-style from compat package)\n              └── Route elements\n                    └── GrafanaRouteWrapper\n                          ├── Auth/RBAC checks\n                          └── GrafanaRoute\n                                ├── ErrorBoundary\n                                ├── Suspense\n                                └── route.component (lazy-loaded)\n```\n\n### Key Files\n\n| File | Role |\n|------|------|\n| `public/app/AppWrapper.tsx` | App entry point, renders the router |\n| `public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx` | Wires up `Router` with `locationService.getHistory()` and `CompatRouter` |\n| `public/app/routes/routes.tsx` | Central route definitions via `getAppRoutes()` |\n| `public/app/core/navigation/GrafanaRoute.tsx` | Route wrapper with auth guards, error boundaries, and suspense |\n| `packages/grafana-runtime/src/services/LocationService.tsx` | The `locationService` singleton |\n| `public/app/core/navigation/patch/interceptLinkClicks.ts` | Document-level `<a>` click interception |\n\n### Router Setup (`RoutesWrapper.tsx`)\n\nThe router is initialized with the v5 `Router` component, receiving a `history` object from `locationService`. It's then wrapped by `CompatRouter` to enable v6 hooks like `useNavigate`, `useLocation`, and `useParams`:\n\n```typescript\n<Router history={locationService.getHistory()}>\n  <LocationServiceProvider service={locationService}>\n    <CompatRouter>\n      {/* AppChrome, Modals, etc. */}\n      {props.routes}\n    </CompatRouter>\n  </LocationServiceProvider>\n</Router>\n```\n\nNo `BrowserRouter` or `createBrowserRouter` is used -- the history instance is managed externally by `locationService`.\n\n### Route Definitions (`routes.tsx`)\n\nRoutes are defined as `RouteDescriptor[]` returned by `getAppRoutes()`. Each descriptor includes:\n\n- **`path`** -- URL pattern\n- **`component`** -- The page component (lazy-loaded via `SafeDynamicImport`, a wrapper around `React.lazy`)\n- **`roles`** -- Optional RBAC role requirements\n- **`chromeless`** -- Whether to hide the app chrome/header\n- **`allowAnonymous`** -- Whether unauthenticated access is permitted\n\nFeature areas contribute their own routes via dedicated functions like `getAlertingRoutes()`, `getPluginCatalogRoutes()`, `getDataConnectionsRoutes()`, etc.\n\n### Route Guards (`GrafanaRoute.tsx`)\n\n`GrafanaRouteWrapper` runs auth checks before rendering:\n\n1. **Anonymous access check** -- If the route doesn't allow anonymous access and the user isn't signed in, redirect to `/login`\n2. **RBAC role check** -- If `roles` are specified, verify the user has at least one of them, otherwise redirect to `/`\n3. **Render** -- Wrap the component in an `ErrorBoundary` and `Suspense` for lazy loading\n\n### `locationService` vs `useNavigate`\n\n**`locationService`** is a singleton that wraps the `history` library:\n\n```typescript\nlocationService.push('/path')              // Navigate\nlocationService.replace('/path')           // Replace history entry\nlocationService.partial({ key: 'value' })  // Update query params\nlocationService.getHistory()               // Returns the history instance\n```\n\nIt also powers **link click interception** -- a document-level handler intercepts all `<a>` tag clicks and routes them through `locationService.push()` instead of triggering full page navigations.\n\n**The migration goal** is to move from `locationService.push()` / `locationService.replace()` calls to React Router's `useNavigate()` hook:\n\n```typescript\nimport { useNavigate } from 'react-router-dom-v5-compat';\n\nconst navigate = useNavigate();\nnavigate('/path');\nnavigate('/path', { replace: true });\n```\n\nSome migrations are gated behind feature flags (e.g., `playlistUseNavigate`, `teamsUseNavigate`), while others like provisioning pages have been fully migrated without flags.\n\n### Summary of Current State\n\n- **Router version**: React Router v5 with v6 compat layer\n- **History management**: Centralized via `locationService` singleton\n- **Route auth**: Frontend guards in `GrafanaRouteWrapper`, backend guards in Go middleware\n- **Lazy loading**: All route components use `SafeDynamicImport` (React.lazy wrapper)\n- **Migration status**: Incrementally moving from `locationService` to `useNavigate`, currently ~40% complete\n- **Link handling**: Document-level click interception routes all `<a>` clicks through `locationService`",
