  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "Here's a detailed Mermaid diagram of the architecture. I've broken it into three diagrams to cover different aspects: the component tree, the navigation flow, and the migration state.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Component & Provider Tree\n\nThis shows how React Router and `locationService` are wired together in the component hierarchy.\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    subgraph \"Application Bootstrap\"\n        A[\"AppWrapper<br/><i>public/app/AppWrapper.tsx</i>\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Provider Shell (AppWrapper.render)\"\n        B[\"Provider (Redux store)\"]\n        C[GrafanaContext.Provider]\n        D[ThemeProvider]\n        E[KBarProvider]\n        F[ScopesContextProvider]\n        G[ExtensionRegistriesProvider]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Router Layer (RouterWrapper)\"\n        H[\"Router (react-router-dom v5)<br/><b>history={locationService.getHistory()}</b>\"]\n        I[\"LocationServiceProvider<br/><i>React Context wrapping locationService singleton</i>\"]\n        J[\"CompatRouter<br/><i>react-router-dom-v5-compat</i><br/>Enables v6 hooks: useNavigate, useLocation, useParams\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"App Shell\"\n        K[AppChrome]\n        L[\"Routes + Route<br/><i>react-router-dom-v5-compat</i>\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Per-Route Rendering\"\n        M[\"GrafanaRouteWrapper<br/><i>Auth & RBAC guards</i>\"]\n        N[\"GrafanaRoute<br/><i>ErrorBoundary + Suspense</i>\"]\n        O[\"route.component<br/><i>Lazy-loaded page</i>\"]\n    end\n\n    A --> B --> C --> D --> E --> F --> G\n    G --> H\n    H --> I --> J\n    J --> K --> L\n    L --> M --> N --> O\n\n    style H fill:#f9e79f,stroke:#f39c12,stroke-width:3px\n    style I fill:#aed6f1,stroke:#2980b9,stroke-width:2px\n    style J fill:#a9dfbf,stroke:#27ae60,stroke-width:3px\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Navigation Flow -- `locationService` vs React Router\n\nThis shows the two parallel navigation pathways and how they share the same underlying `history` object.\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TB\n    subgraph \"Shared Foundation\"\n        HIST[\"H.History<br/>(history library)<br/><b>Single source of truth</b><br/><i>Created by HistoryWrapper via<br/>H.createBrowserHistory()</i>\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Legacy Path (locationService singleton)\"\n        LS[\"locationService<br/><i>HistoryWrapper instance</i><br/>packages/grafana-runtime\"]\n        LS_PUSH[\"locationService.push(path)\"]\n        LS_REPLACE[\"locationService.replace(path)\"]\n        LS_PARTIAL[\"locationService.partial(query)\"]\n        LS_OBS[\"locationService.getLocationObservable()<br/><i>BehaviorSubject&lt;Location&gt;</i>\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Legacy Entry Points\"\n        LINK_INTERCEPT[\"interceptLinkClicks<br/><i>Document-level click handler</i><br/>Intercepts all &lt;a&gt; clicks\"]\n        IMPERATIVE[\"Imperative calls<br/><i>Services, non-React code,<br/>class components</i>\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"React Router Path (v6 compat)\"\n        COMPAT[\"CompatRouter<br/><i>Bridges v5 Router to v6 hooks</i>\"]\n        USE_NAV[\"useNavigate()<br/><i>navigate(path)</i>\"]\n        USE_LOC[\"useLocation()\"]\n        USE_PARAMS[\"useParams()\"]\n        NAVIGATE[\"&lt;Navigate to=... /&gt;<br/><i>Declarative redirects</i>\"]\n        LINK[\"&lt;Link to=... /&gt;\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Router (v5)\"\n        ROUTER[\"&lt;Router history={...}&gt;<br/><i>react-router-dom v5</i>\"]\n    end\n\n    %% Legacy path\n    LINK_INTERCEPT -->|\"e.preventDefault() then\"| LS_PUSH\n    IMPERATIVE --> LS_PUSH\n    IMPERATIVE --> LS_REPLACE\n    IMPERATIVE --> LS_PARTIAL\n\n    LS_PUSH -->|\"this.history.push()\"| HIST\n    LS_REPLACE -->|\"this.history.replace()\"| HIST\n    LS_PARTIAL -->|\"this.history.push/replace()\"| HIST\n\n    %% React Router path\n    USE_NAV -->|\"Calls into history\"| HIST\n    NAVIGATE -->|\"Calls into history\"| HIST\n    LINK -->|\"Calls into history\"| HIST\n\n    %% History feeds Router\n    HIST -->|\"getHistory()\"| ROUTER\n    ROUTER -->|\"Provides context\"| COMPAT\n    COMPAT --> USE_NAV\n    COMPAT --> USE_LOC\n    COMPAT --> USE_PARAMS\n\n    %% Observable\n    HIST -->|\"history.listen()\"| LS_OBS\n\n    style HIST fill:#f9e79f,stroke:#f39c12,stroke-width:3px\n    style LS fill:#fadbd8,stroke:#e74c3c,stroke-width:2px\n    style COMPAT fill:#a9dfbf,stroke:#27ae60,stroke-width:2px\n    style USE_NAV fill:#a9dfbf,stroke:#27ae60,stroke-width:2px\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Migration State Machine\n\nThis shows the conceptual migration journey for a component moving from the legacy pattern to the React Router pattern.\n\n```mermaid\nstateDiagram-v2\n    [*] --> Legacy: Component uses locationService\n\n    state Legacy {\n        direction LR\n        ls_push: locationService.push(path)\n        ls_replace: locationService.replace(path)\n        ls_partial: locationService.partial(query)\n        ls_getLocation: locationService.getLocation()\n        ls_getSearch: locationService.getSearchObject()\n    }\n\n    Legacy --> FeatureFlagged: Add feature toggle\\n(e.g. playlistUseNavigate)\n\n    state FeatureFlagged {\n        direction LR\n        check: if (config.featureToggles.xxxUseNavigate)\n        old_path: locationService.push()\n        new_path: navigate() via useNavigate\n        check --> old_path: flag OFF\n        check --> new_path: flag ON\n    }\n\n    FeatureFlagged --> Migrated: Remove flag,\\ndelete legacy code path\n\n    state Migrated {\n        direction LR\n        useNav: useNavigate()\n        useLoc: useLocation()\n        usePar: useParams()\n        useSearch: useSearchParams()\n        nav_comp: Navigate component\n    }\n\n    Legacy --> Migrated: Direct migration\\n(no feature flag)\n\n    Migrated --> [*]\n```\n\n---\n\n### Key Relationship Summary\n\nThe central insight is that **both** `locationService` and React Router's hooks operate on the **same `H.History` instance**:\n\n1. `HistoryWrapper` creates a `history` object via `H.createBrowserHistory()` at module load time (line 44 of `LocationService.tsx`)\n2. This history object is passed to `<Router history={locationService.getHistory()}>` (line 28 of `RoutesWrapper.tsx`)\n3. `CompatRouter` bridges that v5 `Router` to v6 hooks like `useNavigate()`\n4. So whether code calls `locationService.push('/foo')` or `navigate('/foo')`, both ultimately call `history.push('/foo')` on the same object\n\nThis shared-history design is what makes the incremental migration possible -- legacy and modern code paths coexist because they're both writing to and reading from the same navigation state.",
