  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "Here's a comprehensive breakdown of the React Router architecture in this Grafana codebase:\n\n## Version: React Router v5 with v6 Compatibility Layer\n\nThe primary router is **React Router v5 (5.3.4)**, but the codebase is actively migrating toward v6 using the official **`react-router-dom-v5-compat`** bridge package (v6.26.1).\n\n```json\n\"react-router\": \"5.3.4\",\n\"react-router-dom\": \"5.3.4\",\n\"react-router-dom-v5-compat\": \"^6.26.1\",\n```\n\n## How It's Wired Together\n\n### 1. Root-level Router setup (`RoutesWrapper.tsx`)\n\nThe app uses a v5 `<Router>` at the top level, with v5's `history` object sourced from Grafana's `locationService`. Nested inside it is the `<CompatRouter>` from `react-router-dom-v5-compat`, which allows v6 APIs (like `useLocation`, `useNavigate`, `<Routes>`, `<Route>`, `<Navigate>`) to work within a v5 router tree:\n\n```1:55:public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx\nimport { ComponentType, ReactNode, type JSX } from 'react';\nimport { Router } from 'react-router-dom';\nimport { CompatRouter } from 'react-router-dom-v5-compat';\n// ...\nexport function RouterWrapper(props: RouterWrapperProps) {\n  return (\n    <Router history={locationService.getHistory()}>\n      <LocationServiceProvider service={locationService}>\n        <CompatRouter>\n          {/* ... app shell ... */}\n        </CompatRouter>\n      </LocationServiceProvider>\n    </Router>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Route Definitions (`AppWrapper.tsx` and `routes.tsx`)\n\nRoutes are defined as an array of `RouteDescriptor` objects (a Grafana-specific type), then rendered using v6's `<Routes>` and `<Route>` components:\n\n```80:93:public/app/AppWrapper.tsx\n  renderRoute = (route: RouteDescriptor) => {\n    return (\n      <Route\n        caseSensitive={route.sensitive === undefined ? false : route.sensitive}\n        path={route.path}\n        key={route.path}\n        element={<GrafanaRouteWrapper route={route} />}\n      />\n    );\n  };\n\n  renderRoutes() {\n    return <Routes>{getAppRoutes().map((r) => this.renderRoute(r))}</Routes>;\n  }\n```\n\nThe `getAppRoutes()` function in `routes.tsx` returns all route definitions with paths, components (lazy-loaded via `SafeDynamicImport`), role requirements, and other metadata.\n\n### 3. Route Wrapper (`GrafanaRoute.tsx`)\n\nEach route is wrapped with `GrafanaRouteWrapper`, which uses **v6 hooks** (`useLocation`, `useParams` from `react-router-dom-v5-compat`) for auth checks, role gating, and then renders `GrafanaRoute` which handles page analytics, error boundaries, and suspense for code-splitting:\n\n```64:89:public/app/core/navigation/GrafanaRoute.tsx\nexport function GrafanaRouteWrapper({ route }: Pick<Props, 'route'>) {\n  const location = useLocation();\n  const params = useParams();\n  // ... auth and role checks ...\n  return <GrafanaRoute route={route} location={location} />;\n}\n```\n\n### 4. Two Navigation Paradigms Coexist\n\nThe codebase has **two ways** to perform navigation:\n\n**Legacy: `locationService`** - A Grafana abstraction that wraps a `history` instance and provides imperative navigation methods like `.push()`, `.replace()`, `.partial()`. This is used extensively throughout the codebase (~200+ files):\n\n```typescript\nimport { locationService } from '@grafana/runtime';\nlocationService.push('/some/path');\nlocationService.partial({ editview: 'theme' });\n```\n\n**Modern: `useNavigate`** from `react-router-dom-v5-compat` - The React Router v6 hook-based approach. This is being adopted in newer code (~25+ files, mostly in provisioning, alerting, and admin features):\n\n```typescript\nimport { useNavigate } from 'react-router-dom-v5-compat';\nconst navigate = useNavigate();\nnavigate('/some/path');\n```\n\n### 5. Migration State\n\nThe codebase is **mid-migration** from v5 to v6. Key indicators:\n\n- The comment in `routes.tsx` explicitly says: _\"This will be unnecessary once/when we upgrade to React Router v6 and start using `<Routes>` instead.\"_\n- `<Routes>` and `<Route>` (v6 components) are already used via the compat layer for rendering route definitions\n- `useLocation`, `useParams`, and `Navigate` all come from `react-router-dom-v5-compat`\n- `locationService` is still the dominant navigation mechanism, but `useNavigate` is being adopted in newer feature code\n- The e2e test plugins already use `react-router-dom` v6 (`^6.22.0`)\n\n### Summary Table\n\n| Aspect | Current State |\n|---|---|\n| **Router version** | v5 (5.3.4) primary, v6 via compat layer |\n| **Root router** | v5 `<Router history={...}>` with `<CompatRouter>` |\n| **Route rendering** | v6 `<Routes>` / `<Route>` |\n| **Navigation hooks** | v6 `useLocation`, `useParams`, `useNavigate` (via compat) |\n| **Imperative navigation** | `locationService.push/replace/partial` (legacy, dominant) |\n| **Migration direction** | v5 `locationService` → v6 `useNavigate` |",
