{
  "conversation_id": "3a479831-6e02-4850-985a-ef7091929941",
  "generation_id": "7a87b162-db7c-4edd-bcc3-be2782aae5f2",
  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "Here is a comprehensive overview of the codebase and its router architecture.\n\n---\n\n## Grafana Codebase Overview\n\nGrafana is a large **Go + TypeScript monorepo** with a clear separation of concerns:\n\n| Directory | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `pkg/` | Go backend — APIs, services, data stores, authentication |\n| `public/app/` | React/TypeScript frontend — the single-page application |\n| `packages/` | Shared npm packages (`grafana-data`, `grafana-runtime`, `grafana-ui`, etc.) |\n| `scripts/` | Build tooling (Webpack 5 configs) |\n| `e2e-playwright/` | End-to-end tests |\n| `apps/` | Standalone Grafana sub-applications |\n\n### Frontend Structure (`public/app/`)\n\n- **`core/`** — Core infrastructure: navigation, hooks, services, the `AppChrome` shell\n- **`features/`** — ~54 feature modules (dashboards, explore, alerting, plugins, admin, playlists, etc.)\n- **`routes/`** — Route definitions and the root `RouterWrapper`\n- **`plugins/`** — Built-in datasource and panel plugins\n- **`store/`** — Redux store configuration\n\nThe build uses **Webpack 5** with **Yarn 4 workspaces**, **Nx** for task orchestration, and **TypeScript 5.9**.\n\n---\n\n## Router Architecture\n\n### Version: React Router v5 + v6 Compatibility Bridge\n\nThe app runs on **React Router v5 (5.3.4)** but is actively migrating to v6 via the **`react-router-dom-v5-compat`** (v6.26.1) bridge package. Both APIs coexist.\n\n### The `LocationService` — Grafana's Navigation Abstraction\n\nThe central piece is `LocationService`, a **singleton** defined in `packages/grafana-runtime` that wraps the `history` library. Its implementation class is `HistoryWrapper`:\n\n```mermaid\nclassDiagram\n    class LocationService {\n        <<interface>>\n        +push(location) void\n        +replace(location) void\n        +partial(query, replace?) void\n        +reload() void\n        +getHistory() History\n        +getLocation() Location\n        +getSearch() URLSearchParams\n        +getSearchObject() UrlQueryMap\n        +getLocationObservable() Observable~Location~\n    }\n\n    class HistoryWrapper {\n        -history: History\n        -locationObservable: BehaviorSubject~Location~\n        +constructor(history?)\n        +push(location) void\n        +replace(location) void\n        +partial(query, replace?) void\n        +reload() void\n        +getHistory() History\n        +getLocation() Location\n        +getSearch() URLSearchParams\n        +getSearchObject() UrlQueryMap\n        +getLocationObservable() Observable~Location~\n    }\n\n    class History {\n        <<history npm package>>\n        +location: Location\n        +push(path) void\n        +replace(path) void\n        +listen(callback) void\n    }\n\n    LocationService <|.. HistoryWrapper : implements\n    HistoryWrapper --> History : wraps\n    HistoryWrapper --> BehaviorSubject : emits location changes\n```\n\nKey methods:\n- **`push(path)`** / **`replace(path)`** — full navigation\n- **`partial(query, replace?)`** — merges/removes query parameters while preserving the current pathname\n- **`getHistory()`** — returns the raw `history` object that React Router's `<Router>` consumes\n- **`getLocationObservable()`** — RxJS `BehaviorSubject` for non-React subscribers\n\n### How LocationService Connects to React Router\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    subgraph \"Module Level (Singleton)\"\n        LS[\"locationService<br/>(HistoryWrapper)\"]\n        H[\"history<br/>(createBrowserHistory)\"]\n        LS -->|wraps| H\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"React Component Tree\"\n        R[\"&lt;Router history={locationService.getHistory()}&gt;<br/><i>React Router v5</i>\"]\n        LSP[\"&lt;LocationServiceProvider service={locationService}&gt;<br/><i>React Context</i>\"]\n        CR[\"&lt;CompatRouter&gt;<br/><i>react-router-dom-v5-compat bridge</i>\"]\n        ROUTES[\"&lt;Routes&gt; / &lt;Route&gt;<br/><i>React Router v6 components</i>\"]\n        GRW[\"GrafanaRouteWrapper<br/><i>Auth + RBAC checks</i>\"]\n        GR[\"GrafanaRoute<br/><i>Error boundary + Suspense</i>\"]\n        PAGE[\"Page Component\"]\n    end\n\n    H -->|passed as prop| R\n    R --> LSP\n    LSP --> CR\n    CR --> ROUTES\n    ROUTES --> GRW\n    GRW -->|useLocation, useParams<br/>from v5-compat| GR\n    GR --> PAGE\n\n    style LS fill:#f9f,stroke:#333\n    style CR fill:#ff9,stroke:#333\n```\n\nThe `<CompatRouter>` is the key bridge. It sits inside the v5 `<Router>` and re-exports the router context in a format that v6 hooks (`useNavigate`, `useLocation`, `useParams`, `<Navigate>`) can consume.\n\n### Full Navigation Event Flow\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant User\n    participant DOM as Document (Link Click Interceptor)\n    participant LS as locationService (HistoryWrapper)\n    participant Hist as history (browser history)\n    participant RR as React Router\n    participant GRW as GrafanaRouteWrapper\n    participant Chrome as AppChromeService\n    participant Page as Page Component\n\n    Note over User, Page: Path 1: User clicks an <a> tag\n\n    User->>DOM: Click <a href=\"/d/abc\">\n    DOM->>DOM: interceptLinkClicks()<br/>Strip base URL, validate\n    DOM->>LS: locationService.push(\"/d/abc\")\n    LS->>Hist: history.push(\"/d/abc\")\n    Hist->>Hist: Browser URL updates\n    Hist-->>LS: history.listen() fires\n    LS-->>LS: locationObservable.next(newLocation)\n    Hist-->>RR: React Router detects change\n    RR->>GRW: Match route, render wrapper\n    GRW->>GRW: Auth check (isSignedIn?)<br/>Role check (hasRole?)\n    GRW->>Chrome: chrome.setMatchedRoute(route)\n    GRW->>Page: Render page component\n\n    Note over User, Page: Path 2: Programmatic navigation\n\n    Page->>LS: locationService.partial({tab: \"settings\"})\n    LS->>LS: Merge query params<br/>renderUrl(pathname, mergedQuery)\n    LS->>Hist: history.push(\"/d/abc?tab=settings\")\n    Note right of Hist: Same flow continues as above\n\n    Note over User, Page: Path 3: useNavigate (v6 migration)\n\n    Page->>RR: const navigate = useNavigate()<br/>navigate(\"/d/abc\")\n    RR->>Hist: history.push(\"/d/abc\")\n    Note right of Hist: Same flow continues as above\n```\n\n### The Two Navigation Paradigms\n\nThe codebase has two coexisting navigation patterns:\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    subgraph \"Legacy Pattern (dominant, ~200+ files)\"\n        A1[\"Import locationService<br/>from @grafana/runtime\"]\n        A2[\"locationService.push('/path')\"]\n        A3[\"locationService.partial({key: 'val'})\"]\n        A1 --> A2\n        A1 --> A3\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Modern Pattern (growing, ~25+ files)\"\n        B1[\"Import useNavigate<br/>from react-router-dom-v5-compat\"]\n        B2[\"const navigate = useNavigate()\"]\n        B3[\"navigate('/path')\"]\n        B1 --> B2\n        B2 --> B3\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Shared Foundation\"\n        H[\"history object<br/>(createBrowserHistory)\"]\n    end\n\n    A2 --> H\n    A3 --> H\n    B3 --> H\n\n    style A1 fill:#fdd,stroke:#c33\n    style B1 fill:#dfd,stroke:#3c3\n```\n\nBoth patterns ultimately call methods on the **same `history` instance**, so they are interoperable. The `locationService` singleton owns the `history` object and passes it to `<Router>`, so whether you navigate via `locationService.push()` or `useNavigate()`, the same history is mutated and React Router re-renders accordingly.\n\n### Link Click Interception\n\nAn often-overlooked piece: Grafana registers a **document-level click handler** (`interceptLinkClicks`) that catches all `<a>` tag clicks and routes them through `locationService.push()` instead of triggering full-page navigations. This is how anchor tags work as SPA navigations without every component needing to use `<Link>`.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    CLICK[\"User clicks any &lt;a&gt; tag\"] --> CHECK{Has target=_blank?<br/>Ctrl/Cmd held?<br/>External URL?}\n    CHECK -->|Yes| BROWSER[\"Browser handles normally<br/>(new tab / external)\"]\n    CHECK -->|No| STRIP[\"Strip appSubUrl base path\"]\n    STRIP --> ORG{Org change?<br/>(/profile/switch-org)}\n    ORG -->|Yes| RELOAD[\"window.location.href = href<br/>(full page reload)\"]\n    ORG -->|No| PUSH[\"locationService.push(href)<br/>(SPA navigation)\"]\n    PUSH --> ROUTER[\"React Router re-renders\"]\n```\n\n### Route Definition Pattern\n\nRoutes are defined as `RouteDescriptor` objects — a Grafana-specific type — returned by `getAppRoutes()` in `routes.tsx`. They are then rendered using v6 `<Routes>` / `<Route>` in `AppWrapper.tsx`:\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    RD[\"RouteDescriptor[]<br/>{ path, component, roles, chromeless }\"]\n    RD --> MAP[\"getAppRoutes().map(r => &lt;Route&gt;)\"]\n    MAP --> ROUTES[\"&lt;Routes&gt;<br/>(React Router v6)\"]\n    ROUTES --> GRW[\"&lt;GrafanaRouteWrapper&gt;<br/>Auth + RBAC gate\"]\n    GRW --> GR[\"&lt;GrafanaRoute&gt;<br/>ErrorBoundary + Suspense\"]\n    GR --> PAGE[\"Lazy-loaded page component<br/>(SafeDynamicImport)\"]\n```\n\nComponents are **code-split** via `SafeDynamicImport` (dynamic `import()`) and rendered inside a `<Suspense>` boundary with a loading fallback.\n\n### Summary\n\n| Aspect | Details |\n|---|---|\n| **Primary router** | React Router v5 (5.3.4) |\n| **Migration bridge** | `react-router-dom-v5-compat` (v6.26.1) |\n| **Navigation abstraction** | `locationService` singleton wrapping `history` |\n| **History type** | `createBrowserHistory` from the `history` package |\n| **Route rendering** | v6 `<Routes>` / `<Route>` (via compat layer) |\n| **Hooks in use** | v6 `useLocation`, `useParams`, `useNavigate` (from compat) |\n| **Dominant nav pattern** | `locationService.push()` / `.partial()` (~200+ files) |\n| **Modern nav pattern** | `useNavigate()` (~25+ files, growing) |\n| **Link handling** | Document-level `interceptLinkClicks` listener |\n| **Observable support** | RxJS `BehaviorSubject` on location changes |\n| **Migration direction** | v5 singleton → v6 hooks |",
