  "text": "Here's a breakdown of all the files relevant to the Bookmarks page UI, organized by layer:\n\n---\n\n### Core Page Component\n\n- **`public/app/features/bookmarks/BookmarksPage.tsx`** — The main page component. Contains the layout grid, empty state, and renders each bookmark as a card. This is the primary file you'd edit for page-level UI changes (layout, empty state messaging, card arrangement).\n\n### Route Registration\n\n- **`public/app/routes/routes.tsx`** (around line 537) — Registers the `/bookmarks` route and lazy-loads `BookmarksPage`. You'd only touch this if you need to change the URL path or add route-level guards.\n\n### Data Fetching & Hooks\n\n- **`public/app/core/components/AppChrome/MegaMenu/hooks.ts`** — The `usePinnedItems` hook that fetches the user's bookmarked URLs from their saved preferences via the RTK Query `useGetUserPreferencesQuery` hook. Relevant if you want to change what data is available to the page.\n\n### Utility Functions\n\n- **`public/app/core/components/AppChrome/MegaMenu/utils.ts`** — Contains `findByUrl()` (line 161), which resolves a bookmarked URL to its full `NavModelItem` from the nav tree. Also contains bookmark-related logic in `getActiveItem()` and `enrichWithInteractionTracking()`.\n\n### Card Component\n\n- **`public/app/core/components/NavLandingPage/NavLandingPageCard.tsx`** — The individual card component used to render each bookmark. Controls card layout, description truncation, and category-based color styling. Note this component is shared with other landing pages, so changes here affect more than just bookmarks.\n- **`public/app/core/components/NavLandingPage/NavLandingPageCard.test.tsx`** — Tests for the card component.\n\n### Page Shell\n\n- **`public/app/core/components/Page/Page.tsx`** — The generic `Page` wrapper used via `<Page navId=\"bookmarks\">`. Controls page header, tabs, scrolling, and layout. Changes here are wide-reaching.\n\n### Redux State (Nav Tree / Bookmarks)\n\n- **`public/app/core/reducers/navBarTree.ts`** (line 54) — The `setBookmark` reducer action that manages adding/removing bookmarks in the nav tree Redux state. Relevant if you're changing how bookmarks are stored or structured.\n\n### MegaMenu Integration\n\n- **`public/app/core/components/AppChrome/MegaMenu/MegaMenu.tsx`** (around line 44) — Where bookmarked items are populated as children of the `bookmarks` nav node in the sidebar mega menu. Relevant if your changes need to be reflected in the sidebar too.\n\n### i18n / Translations\n\n- **`public/locales/en-US/grafana.json`** — Contains the `bookmarks-page.empty.message` and `bookmarks-page.empty.tip` translation keys. Update here if you change any user-facing text.\n- Other locale files under `public/locales/*/grafana.json` would need corresponding updates for full internationalization.\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Scoping\n\nFor **UI-only changes to the Bookmarks page**, you'll most likely work within:\n\n| File | When to edit |\n|---|---|\n| `BookmarksPage.tsx` | Layout, grid styling, empty state, which props pass to cards |\n| `NavLandingPageCard.tsx` | Card appearance (shared component — be cautious) |\n| `hooks.ts` | Changing what bookmark data is fetched |\n| `utils.ts` (`findByUrl`) | Changing how URLs resolve to nav items |\n| `en-US/grafana.json` | Any text/copy changes |\n\nThe remaining files (`routes.tsx`, `navBarTree.ts`, `MegaMenu.tsx`, `Page.tsx`) are structural/integration files you'd only need if your changes extend beyond the page itself.",
