  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "Here is a comprehensive overview.\n\n---\n\n## Grafana Codebase Overview\n\nGrafana is a large monorepo with a **Go backend** and a **React/TypeScript frontend**, organized as follows:\n\n| Directory | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `public/app/` | Main frontend application — features, routing, core infra |\n| `pkg/` | Go backend — API handlers, services, plugins, storage, TSDB |\n| `packages/` | Shared npm packages (monorepo): `grafana-ui`, `grafana-data`, `grafana-runtime`, `grafana-api-clients`, etc. |\n| `apps/` | Standalone application entry points |\n| `e2e/`, `e2e-playwright/` | End-to-end tests |\n| `conf/`, `devenv/` | Configuration and dev environment tooling |\n\nThe frontend is feature-oriented — `public/app/features/` contains 50+ feature modules (`alerting/`, `dashboard-scene/`, `explore/`, `bookmarks/`, `plugins/`, etc.), each self-contained with their own components, services, and routes.\n\n---\n\n## React Router Architecture\n\n### Version & Compatibility Layer\n\nGrafana is in the middle of a **React Router v5 → v6 migration**:\n\n- `react-router-dom`: **5.3.4** (legacy, still present)\n- `react-router-dom-v5-compat`: **^6.26.1** (the compatibility bridge — **primary usage**)\n\nThe v5-compat package lets the codebase use **v6 APIs** (`useNavigate`, `useLocation`, `useParams`, `<Routes>`, `<Route element={...}>`) while still running on top of a v5 `<Router>` with a `history` object.\n\n### Router Hierarchy\n\nThe top-level setup lives in `public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx`:\n\n```\n<Router history={locationService.getHistory()}>     ← v5 Router with history object\n  <LocationServiceProvider service={locationService}>\n    <CompatRouter>                                   ← v5-compat bridge for v6 APIs\n      {props.routes}                                 ← Route tree rendered here\n    </CompatRouter>\n  </LocationServiceProvider>\n</Router>\n```\n\nKey takeaway: the v5 `Router` sits at the root providing `history`, and `CompatRouter` wraps everything to enable v6 hooks.\n\n### Route Definitions\n\nRoutes are declared in `public/app/routes/routes.tsx` as an array of `RouteDescriptor` objects:\n\n```typescript\nexport interface RouteDescriptor {\n  path: string;\n  component: GrafanaRouteComponent;\n  roles?: () => string[];\n  chromeless?: boolean;\n  sensitive?: boolean;\n  allowAnonymous?: boolean | ((params) => boolean);\n}\n```\n\nThese descriptors are collected from multiple sources — core routes, feature routes (e.g. `getAlertingRoutes()`, `getProfileRoutes()`), plugin routes (`getAppPluginRoutes()`), and an `extraRoutes` array for enterprise extensions. They're all merged in `getAppRoutes()`.\n\nIn `AppWrapper.tsx`, each descriptor is mapped to a v6 `<Route>`:\n\n```typescript\n<Route\n  path={route.path}\n  key={route.path}\n  element={<GrafanaRouteWrapper route={route} />}\n/>\n```\n\nAll routes are wrapped in a `<Routes>` component (v6 API).\n\n### GrafanaRouteWrapper\n\n`public/app/core/navigation/GrafanaRoute.tsx` is the wrapper applied to every route. It handles:\n\n- **Authentication checks** via frontend auth service\n- **Role-based access control** from the route descriptor\n- **Error boundaries** (`GrafanaRouteError`)\n- **Suspense/lazy loading** (`GrafanaRouteLoading`)\n- **Body class management** for per-page styling\n- **Query parameter parsing** via `locationSearchToObject()`\n\nIt uses `useLocation()` and `useParams()` from the v5-compat package.\n\n### Navigation: Two Coexisting Patterns\n\n#### 1. `locationService` (legacy, still dominant)\n\nDefined in `packages/grafana-runtime/src/services/LocationService.tsx`, this is a **singleton** wrapping the `history` v4 library:\n\n```typescript\nlocationService.push('/dashboards');\nlocationService.partial({ editview: 'settings' });\nlocationService.replace('/');\nlocationService.getLocation();    // current H.Location\nlocationService.getHistory();     // underlying history object\n```\n\nIt also exposes an RxJS `Observable<Location>` for reactive location tracking. This is used in **100+ files** across the codebase.\n\n#### 2. `useNavigate()` (new pattern, growing)\n\n```typescript\nimport { useNavigate } from 'react-router-dom-v5-compat';\nconst navigate = useNavigate();\nnavigate('/playlists');\nnavigate('/playlists', { replace: true });\n```\n\nCurrently used in ~20 files, mostly in newer features like `provisioning/`. The migration from `locationService.push()` to `useNavigate()` is **gradual and ongoing**.\n\n#### Link Interception\n\n`public/app/core/navigation/patch/interceptLinkClicks.ts` intercepts `<a>` tag clicks globally to perform SPA navigation via `locationService.push()` instead of full page reloads.\n\n### Navigation Utilities\n\n`public/app/core/navigation/` provides:\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `hooks.ts` | `useUrlParams()` — query param read/write hook |\n| `GrafanaRoute.tsx` | Route wrapper (auth, roles, error boundaries) |\n| `GrafanaRouteError.tsx` | Error boundary for route rendering |\n| `GrafanaRouteLoading.tsx` | Suspense fallback |\n| `interceptLinkClicks.ts` | Global SPA link interception |\n| `types.ts` | Route-related TypeScript types |\n\n### Plugin Routes\n\nPlugin apps get their own routing via `AppRootPage` (`public/app/features/plugins/components/AppRootPage.tsx`), which dynamically loads plugin root components and manages plugin-specific navigation models using the same v5-compat hooks.\n\n### Migration Status Summary\n\n| Pattern | Files | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| `locationService.*` calls | ~100+ | Legacy, still dominant |\n| `react-router-dom-v5-compat` hooks | ~150+ | Active, used for `useLocation`, `useParams`, etc. |\n| `useNavigate()` | ~20 | New standard, used in recent features |\n| `react-router-dom` (v5 direct) | Minimal | Only the root `<Router>` |\n\nThe codebase is in a **transitional state**: the v5 `Router` + v5-compat bridge is the runtime foundation, v6 APIs are used for route definitions and hooks, and navigation is gradually migrating from the imperative `locationService` singleton to the React Router `useNavigate` hook.",
