  "text": "Here's the diagram and analysis.\n\n---\n\n## React Router v5 → v6 Compatibility Layer\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TB\n    subgraph \"Application Shell\"\n        AW[\"AppWrapper<br/><i>public/app/AppWrapper.tsx</i>\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Provider Stack (v5 Foundation)\"\n        R[\"&lt;Router history={locationService.getHistory()}&gt;<br/><b>react-router-dom v5</b>\"]\n        LSP[\"&lt;LocationServiceProvider&gt;\"]\n        CR[\"&lt;CompatRouter&gt;<br/><b>react-router-dom-v5-compat</b><br/><i>Bridge: enables v6 APIs on v5 core</i>\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Route Rendering (v6 APIs)\"\n        ROUTES[\"&lt;Routes&gt; + &lt;Route element={...}&gt;<br/><i>v6 declarative routing</i>\"]\n        GRW[\"GrafanaRouteWrapper<br/><i>Auth, roles, redirect guards</i>\"]\n        GR[\"GrafanaRoute<br/><i>Error boundary, Suspense, pageview</i>\"]\n        PAGE[\"Page Component\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"History Layer\"\n        HS[\"history v4<br/><i>H.createBrowserHistory()</i>\"]\n        LS[\"locationService (singleton)<br/><i>packages/grafana-runtime/src/services/LocationService.tsx</i>\"]\n        OBS[\"RxJS Observable&lt;Location&gt;\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Navigation APIs (coexisting)\"\n        direction LR\n        LEGACY[\"<b>Legacy: locationService</b><br/>locationService.push()<br/>locationService.replace()<br/>locationService.partial()<br/><i>~150+ call sites</i>\"]\n        MODERN[\"<b>Modern: useNavigate()</b><br/>navigate(path)<br/>navigate(path, {replace})<br/><i>~25 files</i>\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"v6-Compat Hooks (widely adopted)\"\n        UL[\"useLocation()\"]\n        UP[\"useParams()\"]\n        UN[\"useNavigate()\"]\n        NAV[\"&lt;Navigate /&gt;\"]\n    end\n\n    AW --> R\n    R --> LSP\n    LSP --> CR\n    CR --> ROUTES\n    ROUTES --> GRW\n    GRW -->|\"useLocation(), useParams()\"| GR\n    GR --> PAGE\n\n    HS --> LS\n    LS -->|\"getHistory()\"| R\n    LS --> OBS\n\n    CR -.->|\"unlocks\"| UL\n    CR -.->|\"unlocks\"| UP\n    CR -.->|\"unlocks\"| UN\n    CR -.->|\"unlocks\"| NAV\n\n    LEGACY -->|\"calls\"| LS\n    MODERN -->|\"provided by\"| UN\n\n    style R fill:#e74c3c,color:#fff\n    style CR fill:#f39c12,color:#fff\n    style ROUTES fill:#27ae60,color:#fff\n    style GRW fill:#27ae60,color:#fff\n    style LEGACY fill:#e74c3c,color:#fff\n    style MODERN fill:#27ae60,color:#fff\n    style LS fill:#e74c3c,color:#fff\n    style HS fill:#e74c3c,color:#fff\n```\n\n**Color key:** Red = v5/legacy layer, Orange = compatibility bridge, Green = v6/modern layer.\n\n### How the Compatibility Layer Works\n\n1. **`<Router history={...}>`** (v5) sits at the root, consuming a `history` v4 object from `locationService.getHistory()`\n2. **`<CompatRouter>`** wraps the children, bridging v5's context into v6's context — this is what unlocks `useNavigate()`, `useLocation()`, `useParams()`, and `<Navigate />`\n3. **`<Routes>` + `<Route element={...}>`** use v6 declarative syntax for route matching\n4. **`locationService`** is the legacy singleton that wraps `history` v4 directly. It still drives the underlying `<Router>` and is used for navigation in ~150+ call sites\n\nThe bridge means both `locationService.push('/foo')` and `navigate('/foo')` ultimately mutate the **same** `history` instance, so they're interoperable.\n\n---\n\n## Primary Files for Migration\n\n### Tier 1: Core Infrastructure (change these to complete the migration)\n\n| File | Role | Migration Action |\n|---|---|---|\n| `public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx` | Router hierarchy | Replace `<Router>` + `<CompatRouter>` with v6 `<BrowserRouter>` or `createBrowserRouter` |\n| `packages/grafana-runtime/src/services/LocationService.tsx` | `locationService` singleton | Deprecate/remove; consumers should use `useNavigate()` and `useLocation()` |\n| `public/app/AppWrapper.tsx` | Route rendering with `<Routes>` | Already uses v6 APIs — minimal changes needed |\n| `public/app/core/navigation/GrafanaRoute.tsx` | Route wrapper | Already uses v5-compat hooks — swap imports to `react-router-dom` v6 |\n| `public/app/core/navigation/hooks.ts` | `useUrlParams()` | Remove `locationService.partial()` dependency; use `useSearchParams()` from v6 |\n\n### Tier 2: Highest-Impact Consumer Areas (~150+ `locationService` call sites)\n\nThese are the feature areas with the most `locationService.push/replace/partial` calls to migrate:\n\n| Feature Area | Approx. Call Sites | Key Files |\n|---|---|---|\n| `dashboard-scene/` | ~30+ | `DashboardScene.tsx`, `NavToolbarActions.tsx`, `keyboardShortcuts.ts`, `PanelEditor.tsx` |\n| `dashboard/` | ~25+ | `DashboardPage.tsx`, `PanelEditor.tsx`, `DashboardSettings.tsx`, `DashNav.tsx`, `getPanelMenu.ts` |\n| `alerting/unified/` | ~15+ | `AlertRuleForm.tsx`, `SilencesEditor.tsx`, `GroupEditPage.tsx`, `GrafanaModifyExport.tsx` |\n| `scopes/` | ~10+ | `ScopesService.ts`, `ScopesSelectorService.ts`, `ScopesNavigationTreeLink.tsx` |\n| `variables/` | ~10+ | `VariableEditorEditor.tsx`, `actions.ts`, `OptionsPicker/actions.test.ts` |\n| `core/services/` | ~15+ | `keybindingSrv.ts` (15 calls alone) |\n\n### Tier 3: Already Migrated (reference patterns)\n\nThe `provisioning/` feature is the best reference — ~25 files already use `useNavigate()`:\n\n| File | Pattern |\n|---|---|\n| `provisioning/Wizard/hooks/useWizardNavigation.ts` | Custom hook wrapping `useNavigate()` |\n| `provisioning/Connection/ConnectionForm.tsx` | Direct `navigate()` in form handlers |\n| `provisioning/components/Dashboards/SaveProvisionedDashboardForm.tsx` | Post-save navigation |\n\n### Recommended Migration Order\n\n1. **Start with leaf components** — files that only call `locationService.push()` once or twice are easy wins (e.g. `UserCreatePage.tsx`, `CreateTeam.tsx`, `PlaylistNewPage.tsx`)\n2. **Tackle `core/services/keybindingSrv.ts`** — 15 `locationService` calls, but it's a non-React service, so it needs a different approach (pass `navigate` as a callback or keep `locationService` as the imperative escape hatch)\n3. **Work through feature areas** by volume: `dashboard/` → `dashboard-scene/` → `alerting/` → `scopes/`\n4. **Last: swap the root** — once all consumers use v6 hooks, replace `<Router>` + `<CompatRouter>` with a native v6 router in `RoutesWrapper.tsx` and remove the `history` v4 dependency\n\nThe `useUrlParams()` hook in `public/app/core/navigation/hooks.ts` is a good canary — it already uses `useLocation()` from v5-compat but falls back to `locationService.partial()` for writes. Migrating it to `useSearchParams()` from v6 would validate the pattern for query param updates.",
