  "text": "Here's the React Router migration status report for the Grafana codebase:\n\n---\n\n## React Router Migration Status\n\n### Overall Progress: ~12–13% (early-to-mid stage)\n\n- **118 non-test files** still use `locationService.push/replace/partial`\n- **17 non-test files** have been migrated to `useNavigate`\n- **1 file** is partially migrated (uses both)\n\n---\n\n### Remaining `locationService` Usage\n\n| Method | Total Files | Non-Test Files |\n|---|---|---|\n| `locationService.push()` | 79 | 62 |\n| `locationService.replace()` | 23 | 17 |\n| `locationService.partial()` | 53 | 49 |\n| **Any of the three** | **143** | **118** |\n\n### Heaviest Areas Still to Migrate\n\n| Feature Area | Files with legacy usage |\n|---|---|\n| `dashboard` | 33 |\n| `dashboard-scene` | 31 |\n| `alerting` | 22 |\n| `core` (navigation/services) | 8 |\n| `scopes` | 6 |\n| `playlist` | 5 |\n| `variables` | 5 |\n| `explore` | 4 |\n| `browse-dashboards` | 3 |\n| `plugins` | 3 |\n\n---\n\n### Already Migrated to `useNavigate`\n\nThe **Provisioning** feature is the most thoroughly migrated (13 files), with a few others scattered across the codebase:\n\n- **Provisioning** — `ProvisioningWizard`, `ConnectionForm`, `ConfigForm`, `DeleteConnectionButton`, folder/dashboard forms, `SyncRepository`, etc.\n- **GOPS** — `ConfigureIRM.tsx`\n- **Alerting** — `ConfirmVersionRestoreModal.tsx` (1 file out of 22 in alerting)\n- **Admin** — `UserCreatePage.tsx`\n\nOne file (`SaveProvisionedDashboardForm.tsx`) is **partially migrated** — it uses both `useNavigate` and `locationService.partial()`.\n\n---\n\n### Feature Flags\n\nTwo migration-related feature flags exist in the generated toggle files:\n\n- **`playlistUseNavigate`**\n- **`browseDashboardsUseNavigate`**\n\nNeither flag appears to be actively referenced in the frontend code yet, suggesting these migrations are defined but not yet implemented. No `teamsUseNavigate` flag was found in the current branch.\n\n---\n\n### Migration Pattern\n\nAll migrated files import `useNavigate` from `react-router-dom-v5-compat` (the v5→v6 bridge), not from `react-router-dom` directly. The typical migration replaces:\n\n```typescript\n// Before\nlocationService.push('/some/path');\nlocationService.replace('/some/path');\n\n// After\nconst navigate = useNavigate();\nnavigate('/some/path');\nnavigate('/some/path', { replace: true });\n```\n\nThe **Dashboard** and **Dashboard Scene** areas together account for 64 files — nearly half of all remaining migration work — making them the critical path for completing this effort.",
